q-pipe = Which character sends one command's output into another command?
q-pipe-why = A pipe (|) connects the output of the command on its left to the input of the command on its right.
q-append = Which adds a command's output to the end of a file, keeping what is already there?
q-append-why = >> appends to the file; a single > replaces what was in it.
q-status = Which variable holds the exit status of the last command?
q-status-why = $? is 0 when the last command succeeded, and another number when it failed.
q-background = Which character at the end of a command runs it in the background?
q-background-why = A trailing & starts the command and gives you the prompt back right away.
q-and = How do you run "make install" only if "make" succeeded?
q-and-why = && runs the second command only when the first one exits with status 0.
q-history = Which shortcut searches your command history as you type?
q-history-why = Ctrl+R searches back through your history; press it again for older matches.
